course: dictionary
lesson: 4004
title: Gape: wide open, or staring
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Gape can mean to stare with your mouth wide open, usually because you are surprised. «The crowd began to gape at the magician.» The clue is that the crowd is watching something amazing, so gape means stare in amazement.
explain: Gape can also mean to be wide open, with nothing staring at all. «A gaping hole appeared in the wall.» Try the swap test: «A wide-open hole appeared in the wall» still makes sense, so gaping means very wide open.
explain: The words around gape often give the clue. «Deep or gaping cuts are closed with stitches» tells you a gaping cut is big and open, which is why a doctor needs to close it. Gape and gaping are the same word in different forms.
fact: Gape means to stare with your mouth wide open, because you are surprised or amazed.
fact: Gape can also mean to be or become wide open, as in «a hole gaped in the wall».
fact: «Gaping» means very wide open, as in «a gaping wound».
fact: In science, the gape of a bird or snake is how wide its beak or mouth can open.
fact: «Crocodiles gape their mouths to let heat escape» when they are too warm, which helps them cool down.
exercise: «Deep or gaping cuts are closed with stitches.» What does gaping mean here? | A cut covered by a soft bandage | *A big, wide-open cut | A cut that feels cold | A tiny, neat scratch
exercise: «Crocodiles are cold-blooded: they bask in the sun to warm up and gape their mouths to let heat escape.» What does gape mean here? | Roar loudly | Close tightly | *Open wide | Swim fast
exercise: Amira says gape always means to shout. Which meaning of gape is correct for staring at a magician? | Fall over in a heap | Run away and hide | *Stare with your mouth wide open in surprise | Shout very loudly
test: In stories, why might a character gape? | *Because they are shocked or astonished | To eat a big meal | To go to sleep early
test: Which phrase means a big, frightening opening? | *A gaping hole | A warm blanket | A sunny afternoon
exam: Which sentence uses gape to mean wide open? | *A gaping hole was cut in the fence | The bus stopped outside the school | The boy laughed and ran off | She whispered a secret to her friend
